Register gateway to ttn console
Go to The Things network console and click on gateway. Click on register gateway
 
Enter gateway EUI and click confirm and add additional information 

 

 
 



Connect Milesight LoRaWAN Gateway to The Things Stack
Connect to the milesight gateway wifi
 
Go to chrome and type in the IPaddresshttps://192.168.1.1 to access the web GUI. Enter the username and password, then click “Login”.
 
After logging the web GUI, youcanview system information and perform configuration of the gateway
 
Go to packet forwarder. In multi destination - Disable embedded ns by clicking on the pen symbol on embedded ns
 
Creating a basic station
Create a new destination by clicking on the add button. Select basicstation Click save
 

Connecting to CUPS
url : https://eu1.cloud.thethings.network:443
go to this url to download the ca file: https://www.thethingsindustries.com/docs/concepts/advanced/root-certificates/
you can download the file from here: click here on isrg rootX1
 
Change the file format to .trust
 
Import the trustfile
 
Import the cups api key you just downloaded.
 
Connecting to an LNS
url: wss://eu1.cloud.thethings.network:8887
CA Files(*trust): you can use the same trustfile
Client keyfile(*key): use the LNS key you downloaded before.
 
Click save and apply.
 
Now go to TTN console the gateway will show it is connected
 

